How to inject knowledge efficiently? Knowledge Infusion Scaling Law for Pre-training Large Language Models Participating in a study on the "Memory Collapse Phenomenon," Liu contributed to the development of a Knowledge Infusion Scaling Law. This research provides a predictive framework for determining the optimal amount of data repetition required to maximize a model's domain-specific memory. The findings offer a technical solution to the performance degradation observed when models are over-exposed to specific knowledge sets during pre-training.

